{"files":[{"content":"#include <cstdio>\n#include <cassert>\n#include <cstddef>\n#include <vector>\n#include <omp.h>\n#include <limits>\n\nint main() {\n    int n, s;\n    if (scanf(\"%d%d\", &n, &s) != 2) return 0;\n\n    assert(s < n);\n    assert(n < 8000);\n    assert(s > 0);\n    assert(n > 0);\n\n    const int width = n - s + 1;\n    std::vector<int> matrix(static_cast<std::size_t>(n) * n);\n    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < matrix.size(); ++i) {\n        scanf(\"%d\", &matrix[i]);\n    }\n\n    long long best = std::numeric_limits<long long>::min();\n\n    #pragma omp parallel reduction(max:best)\n    {\n        const int tid = omp_get_thread_num();\n        const int team = omp_get_num_threads();\n        const int first = width * tid / team;\n        const int last = width * (tid + 1) / team;\n\n        if (first < last) {\n            const int column_count = last - first + s - 1;\n            std::vector<long long> column_sums(column_count, 0);\n\n            for (int r = 0; r < s; ++r) {\n                const std::size_t row = static_cast<std::size_t>(r) * n + first;\n                for (int c = 0; c < column_count; ++c) {\n                    column_sums[c] += matrix[row + c];\n                }\n            }\n\n            for (int top = 0; top < width; ++top) {\n                if (top > 0) {\n                    const std::size_t leaving = static_cast<std::size_t>(top - 1) * n + first;\n                    const std::size_t entering = static_cast<std::size_t>(top + s - 1) * n + first;\n                    for (int c = 0; c < column_count; ++c) {\n                        column_sums[c] += static_cast<long long>(matrix[entering + c]) - matrix[leaving + c];\n                    }\n                }\n\n                long long sum = 0;\n                for (int c = 0; c < s; ++c) sum += column_sums[c];\n                if (sum > best) best = sum;\n\n                for (int start = first + 1; start < last; ++start) {\n                    const int offset = start - first;\n                    sum += column_sums[offset + s - 1] - column_sums[offset - 1];\n                    if (sum > best) best = sum;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    printf(\"%lld\\n\", best);\n    return 0;\n}\n","path":"src/solution.cpp"}],"hypothesis":"Partitioning window start columns into balanced static stripes lets each OpenMP thread maintain its own rolling vertical column sums and scan all top-row positions without per-row work-sharing barriers. This keeps the scan O(N²), uses only O(N + T·S) extra storage, and may reduce synchronization relative to parallelizing every row of windows.","notes":"The input matrix is stored contiguously; each thread owns a disjoint range of window starts, with only the necessary S-1-column overlap in its private rolling sums. Runtime correctness and speed remain for the controller to evaluate.","research":{"queries":[],"urls":[]},"sources_kept":[],"transformations":["Replace the nested matrix vectors with one contiguous row-major vector and use scanf for consistent fast input.","Use a single OpenMP team with a max reduction and balanced static column stripes; each active thread initializes and rolls private vertical sums across top rows, then scans its horizontal windows locally.","Accumulate window intermediates in long long to avoid overflow in partial sums while retaining the required decimal output."]}